<ptxt>Recording Indicator</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0003" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0016" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A303FX_03_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IH400000">
<testtitle>Microphone Check (Recording and Playback of Spoken Voice)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Microphone Check (Recording and Playback of Spoken Voice)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E122550J07" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>After pressing the record switch, speak into the microphone and record the voice.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Turn off the air conditioner airflow before performing the inspection. If air is blowing toward the microphone, noise may be included in the recorded voice.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Press the playback switch and check the recorded voice.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The spoken voice is played back normally without noise, distortion, etc.</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>During playback of the recorded voice, the microphone input level gauge does not respond to the playback sound.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The content spoken during recording is optional.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Recording stops after 5 seconds elapse or when the stop switch is pressed.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>During recording and playback, all switch operations except the stop switch are disabled.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When nothing has been recorded, the playback switch is grayed out.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Playback ends when playback of the recorded content is finished.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test2>
</test1>
<table>
<title>Text in Illustrations</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="0.41in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.72in"/>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*a</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Microphone Input Level Gauge</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*b</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Playback Switch</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*c</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Record Switch</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*d</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Stop Switch</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*e</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Recording Indicator</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0014" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0016" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A303FX_03_0014" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IH600000">
<testtitle>Re-operate (Voice Recognition)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Re-operate (Voice Recognition)</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Pay attention to how you speak and perform the voice recognition operation again.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Voice is recognized normally</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When recognized normally, a talk-back is given.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If unnecessary words ("er", "um", etc.) are added before or after the recognition word, it will be misrecognized.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Voices cannot be recognized if several people speak at the same time.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the speaking speed is extremely fast or slow, the recognition rate may drop significantly.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Recognition may be difficult depending on voice quality. (Hoarse voice due to poor health, etc.)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0009" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0047" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A303FX_03_0009">
<testtitle>Normal (voice recognition may be difficult depending on how the user speaks)</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A303FX_03_0047">
<testtitle>Replace Navigation Receiver Assembly<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001XG5006X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A303FX_03_0016" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IH700000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Navigation Receiver Assembly - Map Light Assembly)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Pre-inspection Preparation</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Disconnect connector D of the navigation receiver assembly.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Disconnect the map light assembly connector.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between each terminal of the connectors of the vehicle wire harness between the navigation receiver assembly and map light assembly.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.49in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.32in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.32in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D5(MACC) - 12(ACC)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D4(MIC+) - 11(MI1+)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D13(MIC-) - 10(MIC-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between each connector terminal of the navigation receiver assembly vehicle side wire harness and body ground.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D5 (MACC) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D4 (MIC+) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D13 (MIC-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D14 (SGND) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10 kΩ or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D3 (SNS2) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0004" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0020" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A303FX_03_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IH500000">
<testtitle>Inspect Navigation Receiver Assembly (MACC, MIC-, SGND)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Pre-inspection Preparation</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Disconnect the map light assembly connector.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Make sure that the navigation receiver assembly connector is connected.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E187122J15" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Voltage Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), with the navigation receiver assembly connector connected, measure the voltage between each terminal and body ground from the back side of the connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D5 (MACC) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>ACC ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>4 to 6 V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), with the navigation receiver assembly connector connected, measure the resistance between each terminal and body ground from the back side of the connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D13 (MIC-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D14 (SGND) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
<table>
<title>Text in Illustrations</title>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="0.41in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.72in"/>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>*a</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<ptxt>Connector connection condition</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Navigation Receiver Assembly)</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0017" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000016A303FX_03_0010" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A303FX_03_0017" proc-id="RM0550J___0000IH800000">
<testtitle>Inspect Telephone Microphone Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70201</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Waveform Inspection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E195390J01" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Turn ACC ON.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), with the map light assembly connector connected, measure the waveform between terminals 11 (MI1+) and 10 (MIC-) from the back side of the connector.</ptxt>
